from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def write(n,s):p=R/n;p.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
S=json.loads((R/'scenes.json').read_text());N=S['estimated_spoken_words'];M=N/182+8/60
write('README.md',f'''# CEH M08 English Editorial Masterclass v1.0\n\n**Sniffing — source_ready.** Complete production source package: 11 chapters, 58 editable scene boards, {N:,} canonical English spoken words, eight original graded questions, and an integrated Northstar capstone. Actual narration, aligned subtitles, all final scene animations, and the final MP4 have not been produced in this package.\n\n## Start here\n\nRead [the common standard](PRODUCTION_STANDARD_v1.0.md), [the full-film agent prompt](AGENT_PROMPT.md), [the course structure](COURSE_STRUCTURE.md), and [the full script](SCRIPT_en-US.md). The standard preserves M04 v3 editorial design, original Tally, Northstar, narration-only 1.5×, and eight 1.000-second zero-PCM holds.\n\nUse the [58-scene visual browser](previews/index.html), [editable 18-slide deck](slides/CEH_M08_Editable_Visual_Lookbook_18slides.pptx), [motion examples](examples/index.html), and [storyboard](STORYBOARD.md) to review the source. Every SVG remains editable. The deck uses native text, shapes, and connectors; original Tally remains an embedded artwork asset.\n\n## Content and evidence\n\n[Official-topic coverage](COVERAGE_MATRIX.md) connects concepts to scene IDs. [Concept connections](CONCEPT_CONNECTIONS.md) explain prerequisites and next uses. [Evidence cards](case/EVIDENCE_CARDS.md) are fictional and labeled SIMULATED OUTPUT. [Student work](ASSESSMENT_STUDENT.md) and [instructor answers](ASSESSMENT_INSTRUCTOR.md) remain separate. [Sources](SOURCES.md) records live retrieval and limits.\n\nSix deterministic synthetic Ethernet PCAP files support actual read-only tcpdump analysis. Every invented campus observation is labeled SIMULATED OUTPUT. Actual parser measurements are separate from fictional events; Wireshark display expressions are documentation-reviewed, not execution-verified. Prepared teaching material establishes no learner progress.\n\n## Build and inspect\n\nPython 3.10+ is required; the editable deck builder needs `python-pptx`, and preview contact sheets need Pillow. Node 22+ and Puppeteer plus Chromium are needed only for browser QA. The scripts support environment-provided paths; no voice model, token, or paid provider is needed for source reconstruction. See [tooling](tooling/README.md).\n\n```bash\npython3 tooling/build_source.py\npython3 tooling/build_companions.py\npython3 tooling/write_docs.py\npython3 tooling/verify_packets.py\npython3 tooling/validate_pack.py\npython3 -m http.server 8077 --bind 127.0.0.1\n```\n\nOpen `http://127.0.0.1:8077/previews/` or `/examples/`. Rebuilding source invalidates old QA/manifests until checks and packaging run again. Existing locked assets, fonts, and vendor files are already bundled. Original upstream M06 access is unnecessary for these build commands.\n\n## Timing and production\n\nAt the planning assumption of 182 effective WPM, speech plus eight quiz seconds is approximately {M:.2f} minutes. This is an estimate, not measured audio or a duration ceiling. Animation explanation and reading holds add time. Four 12-second executable examples demonstrate motion only; they do not imply the film is 48 seconds or that speech was synthesized.\n\n[Voice specification](VOICE_AND_AUDIO.md), [caption contract](production/CAPTION_CONTRACT.md), [render plan](RENDER_PLAN.md), and [QA checklist](QA_CHECKLIST.md) govern the next production layer. No pilot approval is required. Report any real runtime or rendering blocker precisely.\n\n## Validation and rights\n\n[Source QA](validation/source_qa.json), browser checks, visual review, and release manifest establish their named layers. `FILES_SHA256.txt` excludes itself and `PACK_MANIFEST.json` to avoid a circular digest. The external ZIP receipt measures the archive after closure.\n\n[Licenses and provenance](LICENSES_AND_PROVENANCE.md) distinguish user-supplied shared artwork, newly authored course sources, fonts, and GSAP. A source-ready package is distinct from human acceptance and public media release.\n''')
write('START_HERE_zh-TW.md',f'''# CEH M08 Sniffing 製作來源包\n\n目前交付為完整製作來源包：11 章、58 幕、{N:,} 字英文旁白逐字稿、8 題原創分級選擇題與綜合實務作業。實際配音、對齊字幕、全片動畫與 MP4 是下一個製片階段。\n\n1. 閱讀 [初版通則](PRODUCTION_STANDARD_v1.0.md) 與 [AGENT_PROMPT.md](AGENT_PROMPT.md)。\n2. 檢視 [逐字稿](SCRIPT_en-US.md)、[58 幕預覽](previews/index.html) 及 [18 頁可編輯簡報](slides/CEH_M08_Editable_Visual_Lookbook_18slides.pptx)。\n3. 透過 README 的本機伺服器開啟 [四組可拖曳時間軸範例](examples/index.html)。\n4. 執行來源驗證後，交由 Codex / HyperFrames 完成全片製作。\n\n旁白沿用核准的美式英文 `af_heart`、基準速度 0.73，再對語音執行一次 `atempo=1.5`。影片與動畫維持原速。每題完整題幹與 A–D 選項之後，插入恰好 1.000 秒零值 PCM；八題共 8.000 秒。\n\n案例採合成封包，提供可重現的離線 tcpdump 分析；觀測、推論與實際工具量測分開記錄。這份教材完成不等於學習、實作或考試準備度已完成。\n''')
write('AGENT_PROMPT.md','''# Execute the full CEH M08 production workflow\n\nYou are producing CEH Module 08: Sniffing for Northstar Learning Center. Read every root specification, all chapters/scenes/questions/visual JSON, the complete script, storyboard, case evidence, asset licenses, source QA, and the four motion examples before implementation. Treat PRODUCTION_STANDARD_v1.0.md as the adopted series contract.\n\n## Required final result\n\nProduce all 58 genuinely animated scenes across 11 chapters, complete American English narration, synchronized SRT/VTT and burned-in captions, chapter outputs, an editable HyperFrames project, and a final 1920×1080 / 30 fps H.264/AAC MP4. Keep a lossless reference audio mix and a measured timeline. Do not require a short pilot approval. Source boards and four examples are references, not already completed full-film animation.\n\nPreserve M04 v3 warm paper editorial design, original Tally, the exact inherited Northstar map and roles, and locked style hashes. Use the native geometry and semantic relationships as the basis for layered explanation. Avoid a slide parade or a still image presented as animation. Keep all spoken/visual/caption instructional language simple American English. Preserve the complete canonical teaching content and all options and explanations.\n\n## Voice and quizzes\n\nUse the approved local Kokoro af_heart en-US voice at baseline speed 0.73 and exactly one `atempo=1.5` on each spoken clip. Do not speed up the whole film or apply a second tempo pass. Freeze voice/model versions and fingerprints in the production ledger. Respect approved local voice custody; no paid provider or upload is required by this package. A genuinely unavailable dependency is a blocker to report with its precise stage.\n\nUse audio_segments as the authoritative ordering. For each of Q01–Q08, synthesize the complete stem and A–D choices, then insert exactly 48,000 stereo audio frames of zero-valued PCM at 48 kHz. Reveal and narrate the answer only after that 1.000-second buffer. Eight holds total 8.000 seconds. Do not infer final timestamps from the illustrative quiz example's [6,7) interval. Reading holds can be placed elsewhere. Keep music off.\n\n## Production stages\n\n1. Revalidate source, assets, question mapping, and all six synthetic PCAP fixtures. Preserve source fingerprints before making production adaptations.\n2. Inspect the actual HyperFrames installation and read its current skills/CLI help. Freeze dependencies and use local fonts, GSAP, images, and license records.\n3. Split spoken audio into manageable clips without dropping text. Cache by text/voice/model/speed fingerprint. Synthesize baseline clips, process speech once, normalize consistently without clipping, and record measured durations. Apply any approved pronunciation intervention in a synthesis-only ledger.\n4. Build each scene with meaningful orient/explain/reason/hold phases. Derive durations from actual processed speech, necessary motion, and reading time. Preserve caption clearance. Use paused registered timelines and deterministic forward/backward seeking.\n5. Assemble a sample-accurate speech/silence ledger and scene/chapter boundaries. Produce aligned captions against final processed audio; audit complete spoken coverage and keep silent windows free of captions. Never label unmeasured estimated captions as final.\n6. Validate every actual scene and chapter. Technical sample checks are allowed to diagnose problems, without creating a new user approval gate. Render all chapters, then assemble the complete master at video rate 1.0. Use durable logs and resumable fingerprints rather than restarting unrelated completed stages.\n7. Fully decode the actual MP4; verify codecs, 1920×1080, 30 fps, frames, durations, chapter continuity, audio coverage, and no dropped/black intervals. Inspect encoded visual samples spanning every scene, chapter transitions, dense diagrams, all quiz holds, and answer boundaries.\n8. Verify all eight reference zero buffers and actual timeline boundaries. Measure decoded AAC windows separately and disclose boundary residues. Audit speech against the complete source and listen to flagged pronunciation, option letters, and dense terminology.\n9. Package the editable project and provide actual file hashes, logs, QA, remaining human review items, and the master location. Keep source_ready, runtime readiness, rendered output, human acceptance, and public release distinct.\n\n## Educational and evidence boundaries\n\nAll Northstar cards and generated network events are SIMULATED OUTPUT. Read PCAP files offline with numeric output. Do not activate interface capture, packet transmission, spoofing, rogue services, credential collection, or external targets. A binding claim, client acceptance, forwarding, application success, cache state, and impact remain separate claims. Use the offline measurement receipt only as evidence about synthetic bytes. Do not alter the existing 600-question bank or mark learner practice complete.\n\n## Truthful blocker reporting\n\nIf a real blocker prevents a stage, retain completed artifacts and report the failed command, diagnostic path, affected deliverable, and smallest next action. Never claim narration, final captions, all animated scenes, or MP4 complete from a prompt, scaffold, source validation, or four examples. Full human viewing/listening remains a separate acceptance layer even after automated rendering checks pass.\n''')
write('VOICE_AND_AUDIO.md','''# Voice and audio contract\n\nUse local Kokoro `af_heart`, language en-US, baseline synthesis speed 0.73. Freeze the actual model and dependency versions when full production starts. Apply exactly one FFmpeg `atempo=1.5` per spoken clip. The source package contains no generated speech and no voice model weights.\n\nUse 48 kHz stereo PCM for the production timeline. `production/quiz_silence_1s_48k_stereo.wav` contains exactly 48,000 audio frames of signed 16-bit zero PCM in two channels. Duplicate that exact interval at each question's measured position after the full stem and all choices. An audio frame contains both channel samples. Eight holds total 384,000 audio frames.\n\nMeasure raw processed clip duration and report raw WPM. If reporting an edge-trimmed signal estimate, retain internal pauses and disclose the threshold/window/guard and sensitivity; do not alter the approved rate to force a nominal WPM. Use a stable gain target, inspect true peaks, avoid clipping, and record actual loudness measurements. No BGM is included or enabled.\n\nFinal MP4 audio is AAC, with a preserved lossless reference. AAC may produce tiny nonzero decoded samples at boundaries even when the source interval is exactly zero. Measure each full window and interior, report peaks/nonzero counts, and preserve reference proof separately. No final AAC audit exists in this source-only release.\n''')
write('production/CAPTION_CONTRACT.md','''# Caption contract\n\nNo synchronized SRT or VTT is included because speech has not been synthesized. Canonical narration and audio segment order are provided in scenes.json.\n\nAlign captions against the final once-processed voice, not baseline audio. Include every spoken stem, A–D choice, answer, and explanation. Use readable phrase units, at most two lines in the approved lower safe area; validate actual font metrics, reading time, and diagram clearance. Preserve wording and terminology.\n\nNo caption event may overlap a measured silent quiz window. The answer's visual/caption/audio onset occurs after the 1.000-second hold. Maintain per-word or per-segment alignment evidence and a coverage audit linking source text to caption events. Export SRT and VTT plus the burned-in version and inspect encoded samples. Reading speed or overlap issues require a timing/layout correction, not silent deletion of course text.\n''')
write('RENDER_PLAN.md','''# Full-film render plan\n\nCurrent status: source_ready; no complete M08 speech, aligned captions, or final MP4. The next agent executes AGENT_PROMPT.md directly without a short-pilot approval.\n\nUse a local executable project separate from the immutable source release. Freeze source hashes, runtime/tool versions, fonts, voice/model identity, and output profile. Keep chapter IDs C01–C11 and scene IDs S01–S58. Build a timeline from measured speech and sample-accurate silence, then add explicit reading/motion holds outside quiz intervals. No runtime ceiling applies.\n\nEach scene uses native layers with a finite paused registered timeline. Reveal mechanisms and evidence relationships in the narration's order. Validate direct seeks and reverse seeks, initial and final states, text bounds, font loading, asset resolution, and caption safe area. Use chapter-level rendering and input fingerprints to resume safely.\n\nThe full 1920×1080/30 master uses H.264/AAC at video rate 1.0. Preserve a lossless mix, subtitle files, chapters, editable project, provenance, and actual QA. A successful four-example render establishes only those examples. Full chapter decode, complete master decode, frame/duration checks, encoded sampling, and audio/caption coverage establish their named layers. Human acceptance and any external release remain separate.\n\nIf a dependency, voice runtime, storage limit, or renderer fails, record the exact command/error and completed stage. Keep the active logs and resumable artifacts. Do not invent a delivery receipt for a nonexistent MP4.\n''')
write('QA_CHECKLIST.md','''# Acceptance checklist\n\n## Source release\n\n- Check 11 chapter ranges, 58 unique scene IDs, complete script/JSON mirrors, spoken word counts, and visual-copy mappings.\n- Check eight original film questions, A–D choices, two questions each on S54–S57, level distribution, answer keys, and exact segment order.\n- Check the four connected cases, six packet fixtures, filter results, declared observation points and evidence limits against the script.\n- Check all 44 inherited asset hashes and the native SVG/PPTX structures. Inspect all 58 boards and 18 actual deck previews.\n- Execute all four examples with local assets, direct/reverse seeks, missing-resource/error detection, and exact quiz answer boundaries.\n- Read the actual reference WAV: 48,000 frames, 48 kHz, stereo, 16-bit, all samples zero.\n- Verify source manifest, ZIP CRC, extracted manifest, and external archive hash after closure. Record actual counts.\n\n## Full production: next layer\n\n- Validate all actual animated scenes, measured speech, source/audio coverage, final caption alignment, and complete timeline.\n- Validate eight sample-accurate quiz intervals in reference PCM and answer visibility during forward/backward seeking.\n- Render and fully decode chapters/master; inspect encoded visual samples and listen to flagged terminology/options.\n- Measure AAC decoded windows separately from reference zero PCM. Record source/output fingerprints and actual artifact paths.\n- Record full human viewing/listening acceptance independently. Prepared sources establish no learner completion or public release.\n''')
write('LICENSES_AND_PROVENANCE.md','''# Licenses and provenance\n\nThe 44 locked source assets inherit the user-approved M04 v3 design through the original M06 v1.1 package. LOCKED_SOURCE_SHA256.json records their exact bytes. Original M06 ZIP SHA-256: 13398381289734b31525cbd5c0c3afb01170039c7ff4ce8af379e94d3b151ee9. New M08 instruction, narration, evidence cards, packet fixtures and diagrams were authored for this request. Source-build tooling is adapted from the M07 source package; no M07 validation is reused as M08 evidence. No general license for public redistribution of the user's artwork or course branding is inferred.\n\nOriginal Tally is reused as artwork rather than redrawn. Shared color/map/character documents remain inherited references; M08 teaching content is new. The editable SVG/PPTX mechanism text and shapes remain editable; the mascot image is an embedded original asset.\n\nBundled Liberation and DejaVu font files retain their copyright/license notices. The locked historical token file mentions Inter/Arial and no redistributed fonts; that historical byte-level reference remains unchanged. For reproducible M08 previews, the approved local Liberation Sans fallback is frozen with its license. This is a declared runtime fallback, not a new series visual identity.\n\nGSAP is locally bundled with its actual standard-license reference. The source package includes no Kokoro model weights, TTS output, or Python dependency environment. Its model card/license reference supports the future voice workflow only. See licenses/media-ledger.json for adopted asset provenance. Official references are linked, not redistributed as courseware.\n''')
write('STYLE_INHERITANCE.md','# Inheritance and M08 additions\n\nThe 44 locked assets preserve M04 v3 design, original Tally and the Northstar map byte-for-byte. Current timing follows PRODUCTION_STANDARD_v1.0.md. M08 teaching is independently authored; m08_network_extensions.json adds explicit synthetic gateway, DHCP, VLAN and MAC roles without altering inherited identities. M08 props, packet fixtures, mechanism labels and diagrams are new source layers. Preview PNGs are review aids; SVG geometry and PowerPoint text/shapes remain editable.\n')
